EXTENSION "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_CollemLeonis_BoonsHooks" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Through the Aegis - Chapter Six: Collem Leonis boons hooks"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's boons hooks, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t2d37f495a24fcd86f4d6bf ^"Tame Nobleman (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tXe4Ys9soxKIf3ggEm1RCJNO ^"Tame Nobleman"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Tame Nobleman (Major Residents Boon)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Residents"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The magi have had an arrangement with the local vassal to the Count of Mark since the emergence of the Berg-Althena dynasty. In 1220 this is Herr Vorderhagen, and his family has possessed the lands for two generations. While Herr Vorderhagen is the formal lord, the lands are so vast and wild that the magi have fairly free rein away from the settled areas."
    }

    #tfca76d406822f779b2daf2 ^"Hidden Resources (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tARMDefCompatCovenantBoon ^"Covenant Boon"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Hidden Resources (Minor Resources Boon, selected four times)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Resources"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Several different setbacks during the failing Winter years led to a lot of Collem Leonis’ important, magical resources being destroyed, lost, or removed. Throughout the chapter can be found Story Seeds for inspiration to rediscovering portions of these, totaling 1000 Build Points"
    }

    #t6288e35e99cdfcde3179ac ^"Manor Hall (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tARMDefCompatCovenantBoon ^"Covenant Boon"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Manor Hall (Free Buildings Boon)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Free"
            ^"Category" STRING "Buildings"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The primary building of Collem Leonis is an old but well-built rectangular manor hall with thick walls and few entrances."
    }

    #t3c6ed87d7c1b83ea488b9b ^"Aura (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tARMDefCompatCovenantBoon ^"Covenant Boon"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Aura (Minor Site Boon, selected twice)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Site"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The wild, forested hills of Sauerland have been untouched by mundanes for centuries, creating a Magic aura of 5 at the covenant site."
    }

    #teb856548975a019feed8ec ^"Strong Community (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #ts3FmoApodp0dIRHslMJXP1K ^"Strong Community"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Strong Community (Minor Residents Boon)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Residents"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Many covenfolk have worked and lived at Collem Leonis for generations, and others are recruited from the locale. The covenant has protected them from war, sickness, hard winters, and hunger, and they have stood together in hard times, winning glory alongside the magi. This makes it more difficult for outside agencies to infiltrate and spy, which considering the recent re-emergence from isolation into Hermetic society would otherwise be a risk."
    }

    #t6c33b00e70846b7a51b336 ^"Chase (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tlTwzNWW2xYLSRfS3d4JvrAL ^"Chase"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Chase (Minor Surroundings Boon)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Surroundings"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Boon"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The covenant has the right to hunt game, gather resources, and fell trees in an area defined as the special hunting grounds of the Count in the wild, forested hills. For the time being! This agreement is very loose and good relations with Herr Vorderhagen need to be maintained."
    }

    #t67dd6a2f95a9fe296de061 ^"City (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t1McSfe385N10BTPQvBM1FI7 ^"City"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "City (Major Surroundings Hook)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Surroundings"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Originally, the relative closeness to Dortmund was not an issue, but the town’s explosive growth during the latter half of the 12th century resulted in the city becoming a force to be reckoned with. The beneficial effects of increased availability of high quality manufactured goods, information, and even exotic items may become overshadowed by growing guild influence and expansion into the wild areas. Julia of Tremere must work diligently and use her connections to offset these challenges. However, her deep involvement through personal contacts as well as through her extended, mundane family means she risks exposure and possible charges of meddling with mundanes."
    }

    #t9d28eecca158e4efaae23d ^"Mundane Politics (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOQLLSp45vaBEbxsl0ZWt9sJ ^"Mundane Politics"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Mundane Politics (Major External Relations Hook)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "External Relations"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Relations and politics prove an eternal challenge for the sociable magi, having to deal with mundane nobility, church, and guildmasters from chartered towns. The area is a hotbed of warmongering and political maneuvering between the Counts of Mark and Berg, who both know of the magi and want to use them. As yet no breaches of the Code have ever been proven, although the upcoming Tribunal may change this. Ideas for storylines are found in the section The Covenant in Play, later."
    }

    #tf2f7a157b623f2ea2f4ce8 ^"Uncontrolled Portal (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tXMKfwSAy54bZAAfRI4Dv0RQ ^"Uncontrolled Portal"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Uncontrolled Portal (Minor Site Hook, selected twice)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Site"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Seemingly random places in the heavily forested hills and valleys open up to Magical or Faerie regiones without warning and with no discernible pattern. Through these portals come Nordic supernatural creatures, as well as other inexplicable events such as unnatural weather phenomena. These portals are covered in more detail in the section Covenant Buildings later, while sample storylines are found in the section The Covenant in Play."
    }

    #t157cf8d01f76fc784b6e94 ^"Rights and Customs (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYbR0gxixoMP6RT7PK74FTtt ^"Rights and Customs"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Rights and Customs (Minor Residents Hook)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Residents"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Over the many years of Collem Leonis’ existence a good number of local holidays and periodic feasts have become part of daily life. These are now are believed to be unbreakable rules. Old wordings allow a set number of covenfolk, from when the covenant was much larger, to be free from work obligations on specific days. These customs must be honored by the magi or risk severe loyalty issues, even though the dwindling number of servants means that on some days virtually no covenfolk are at work."
    }

    #ta194ffbb99526a60247bd8 ^"Suffrage (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tbIJSCUPwnrECSc1DVJtuY3o ^"Suffrage"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Suffrage (Minor Residents Hook)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Residents"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "It is not unusual for Hermetic magi to consider the two genders equal, and Collem Leonis took this a step further when founding maga Briana ensured equal rights for women were entered into the charter of the covenant. Visitors and outside relations are puzzled by this structure, and if the Church were to investigate this would be considered sinful."
    }

    #tb9c02b1e05a47ed09886c1 ^"Vis Salary (Collem Leonis)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tARMDefCompatCovenantHook ^"Covenant Hook"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Vis Salary (Minor resources Hook)"
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "resources"
            ^"Kind" STRING "Hook"
            ^"Covenant" STRING "Collem Leonis"
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 135
        }
        DESCRIPTION "In accordance with the charter of Collem Leonis the members must adhere to a strict hierarchy and more importantly provide services in order to receive their bi-annual vis grant from the resources owned by the covenant. Since the council has a great deal of freedom to interpret the guidelines in the charter to determine which activities are regarded as services eligible for payment there is a significant advantage to be had from finding a lucrative niche or services to provide."
    }

}
